{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-3-6","title":"prop:dc-ch3-3-6","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":697,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#prop:dc-ch3-3-6","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-9]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"prop:dc-ch3-3-6","line":2017,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[geodesics locally minimize]\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch3-3-6}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise, prop:dc-ch3-2-9}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.6}\n  Let $p\\in M$, $U$ a normal neighborhood of $p$, and $B\\subset U$ a normal ball of\n  center $p$. Let $\\gamma:[0,1]\\to B$ be a geodesic segment with $\\gamma(0)=p$. If\n  $c:[0,1]\\to M$ is any piecewise differentiable curve joining $\\gamma(0)$ to\n  $\\gamma(1)$, then $\\ell(\\gamma)\\le\\ell(c)$, and if equality holds then\n  $\\gamma([0,1])=c([0,1])$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise}\n  Suppose first $c([0,1])\\subset B$. For $t\\ne 0$ write uniquely\n  $c(t)=\\exp_p(r(t)\\,v(t))=f(r(t),t)$, $|v(t)|=1$, $r:(0,1]\\to\\mathbb{R}$ positive\n  piecewise differentiable. Then except at finitely many points\n  $\\frac{dc}{dt}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}r'(t)+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$.\n  By the Gauss lemma $\\langle\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r},\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\rangle=0$\n  and $|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}|=1$, so\n\n  $$\n  \\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|^2=|r'(t)|^2+\\Big|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\Big|^2\\ge|r'(t)|^2,\\qquad\\text{(1)}\n  $$\n\n  $$\n  \\int_\\varepsilon^1\\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|dt\\ge\\int_\\varepsilon^1|r'(t)|dt\\ge r(1)-r(\\varepsilon).\\qquad\\text{(2)}\n  $$\n\n  Letting $\\varepsilon\\to0$ gives $\\ell(c)\\ge r(1)=\\ell(\\gamma)$. If equality holds\n  then $|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}|=0$ and $r'(t)>0$, so $c$ is a monotone\n  reparametrization of $\\gamma$ and $c([0,1])=\\gamma([0,1])$. If $c([0,1])\\not\\subset B$,\n  let $t_1$ be the first time $c(t_1)\\in\\partial B$; with $\\rho$ the radius of $B$,\n  $\\ell(c)\\ge\\ell_{[0,t_1]}(c)\\ge\\rho>\\ell(\\gamma)$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[geodesics locally minimize] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a64632d6368332d332d36\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-normal\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-competitor\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-confinement\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23prop%3Adc-ch3-2-9\">↗ prop:dc-ch3-2-9</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.6</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U$\">$U$</span> a normal neighborhood of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B\\subset U$\">$B\\subset U$</span> a normal ball of center <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span>. Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[0,1]\\to B$\">$\\gamma :[0,1]\\to B$</span> be a geodesic segment with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (0)=p$\">$\\gamma (0)=p$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c:[0,1]\\to M$\">$c:[0,1]\\to M$</span> is any piecewise differentiable curve joining <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (0)$\">$\\gamma (0)$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (1)$\">$\\gamma (1)$</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\ell (\\gamma )\\le \\ell (c)$\">$\\ell (\\gamma )\\le \\ell (c)$</span>, and if equality holds then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma ([0,1])=c([0,1])$\">$\\gamma ([0,1])=c([0,1])$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-competitor\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-radius\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-confinement\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise</a> Suppose first <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c([0,1])\\subset B$\">$c([0,1])\\subset B$</span>. For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t\\ne 0$\">$t\\ne 0$</span> write uniquely <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c(t)=\\exp _p(r(t)\\, v(t))=f(r(t),t)$\">$c(t)=\\exp _p(r(t)\\, v(t))=f(r(t),t)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|v(t)|=1$\">$|v(t)|=1$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r:(0,1]\\to \\mathbb {R}$\">$r:(0,1]\\to \\mathbb {R}$</span> positive piecewise differentiable. Then except at finitely many points <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\frac{dc}{dt}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}r&#x27;(t)+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$\">$\\frac{dc}{dt}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}r&#x27;(t)+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$</span>. By the Gauss lemma <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\langle \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r},\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\rangle =0$\">$\\langle \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r},\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\rangle =0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}|=1$\">$|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}|=1$</span>, so </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|^2=|r&#x27;(t)|^2+\\Big|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\Big|^2\\ge |r&#x27;(t)|^2,\\qquad \\text{(1)}  \\]\">\\[  \\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|^2=|r&#x27;(t)|^2+\\Big|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\Big|^2\\ge |r&#x27;(t)|^2,\\qquad \\text{(1)}  \\]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\int _\\varepsilon ^1\\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|dt\\ge \\int _\\varepsilon ^1|r&#x27;(t)|dt\\ge r(1)-r(\\varepsilon ).\\qquad \\text{(2)}  \\]\">\\[  \\int _\\varepsilon ^1\\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|dt\\ge \\int _\\varepsilon ^1|r&#x27;(t)|dt\\ge r(1)-r(\\varepsilon ).\\qquad \\text{(2)}  \\]</span></p><p>Letting <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\varepsilon \\to 0$\">$\\varepsilon \\to 0$</span> gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\ell (c)\\ge r(1)=\\ell (\\gamma )$\">$\\ell (c)\\ge r(1)=\\ell (\\gamma )$</span>. If equality holds then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}|=0$\">$|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}|=0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$r&#x27;(t)&gt;0$\">$r&#x27;(t)&gt;0$</span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is a monotone reparametrization of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c([0,1])=\\gamma ([0,1])$\">$c([0,1])=\\gamma ([0,1])$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c([0,1])\\not\\subset B$\">$c([0,1])\\not\\subset B$</span>, let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_1$\">$t_1$</span> be the first time <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c(t_1)\\in \\partial B$\">$c(t_1)\\in \\partial B$</span>; with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\rho $\">$\\rho $</span> the radius of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$B$\">$B$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\ell (c)\\ge \\ell _{[0,t_1]}(c)\\ge \\rho &gt;\\ell (\\gamma )$\">$\\ell (c)\\ge \\ell _{[0,t_1]}(c)\\ge \\rho &gt;\\ell (\\gamma )$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-7-descent","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-9","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-9","label":"prop:dc-ch3-2-9"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","label":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#cor:dc-ch3-3-9","title":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9","label":"cor:dc-ch3-3-9"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-bridge-ball"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-lowerbound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-minimizing-interior"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-stronglyconvex-reduction"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist","title":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist","label":"lem:dc-ch3-4-2-speed-dist"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-3-6","title":"prop:dc-ch3-3-6","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[geodesics locally minimize]\n  \\label{prop:dc-ch3-3-6}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise, prop:dc-ch3-2-9}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:3.6}\n  Let $p\\in M$, $U$ a normal neighborhood of $p$, and $B\\subset U$ a normal ball of\n  center $p$. Let $\\gamma:[0,1]\\to B$ be a geodesic segment with $\\gamma(0)=p$. If\n  $c:[0,1]\\to M$ is any piecewise differentiable curve joining $\\gamma(0)$ to\n  $\\gamma(1)$, then $\\ell(\\gamma)\\le\\ell(c)$, and if equality holds then\n  $\\gamma([0,1])=c([0,1])$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\sketch\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise, lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise}\n  Suppose first $c([0,1])\\subset B$. For $t\\ne 0$ write uniquely\n  $c(t)=\\exp_p(r(t)\\,v(t))=f(r(t),t)$, $|v(t)|=1$, $r:(0,1]\\to\\mathbb{R}$ positive\n  piecewise differentiable. Then except at finitely many points\n  $\\frac{dc}{dt}=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}r'(t)+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}$.\n  By the Gauss lemma $\\langle\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r},\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\rangle=0$\n  and $|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial r}|=1$, so\n\n  $$\n  \\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|^2=|r'(t)|^2+\\Big|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\Big|^2\\ge|r'(t)|^2,\\qquad\\text{(1)}\n  $$\n\n  $$\n  \\int_\\varepsilon^1\\Big|\\frac{dc}{dt}\\Big|dt\\ge\\int_\\varepsilon^1|r'(t)|dt\\ge r(1)-r(\\varepsilon).\\qquad\\text{(2)}\n  $$\n\n  Letting $\\varepsilon\\to0$ gives $\\ell(c)\\ge r(1)=\\ell(\\gamma)$. If equality holds\n  then $|\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}|=0$ and $r'(t)>0$, so $c$ is a monotone\n  reparametrization of $\\gamma$ and $c([0,1])=\\gamma([0,1])$. If $c([0,1])\\not\\subset B$,\n  let $t_1$ be the first time $c(t_1)\\in\\partial B$; with $\\rho$ the radius of $B$,\n  $\\ell(c)\\ge\\ell_{[0,t_1]}(c)\\ge\\rho>\\ell(\\gamma)$.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-normal","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-piecewise","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-competitor","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-radial","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-geodesic","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-ray-piecewise","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-confinement-piecewise","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-equality-manifold-piecewise","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#prop:dc-ch3-2-9","title":"prop:dc-ch3-2-9","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-radius","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","title":"lem:dc-ch3-3-6-rayspeed","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}